@startuml strategic-economy
' SPEC: _spec/apps/starchess/core/adjutant/strategic/strategic-economy.puml
' purpose: ADJUTANT (SCRIPT STRATEGIC) — Command Center economy reacts to the known-vs-seen dials.
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/ai/strategic/strategies/economy.ts
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/ai/strategic/deployLookahead.ts
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/ai/strategies/economy.ts
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/__tests__/strategic/economy.test.ts
' see also: ../weight-ladder.puml (these dials in the full roster)
' see also: ../cc-focus.puml (whose CC guess the warp bonus reads)
' see also: _spec/packages/starchess-core/deploy-reach.puml (the non-goal split)
!include ../../../../../themes/proveo.puml

skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left

title StarChess · Strategic economy — deploy dials on known-vs-seen

package "Inputs" {
  database "kvs\nknown · scouted · captured" as KVS <<db>>
  component "bank · unit mix · king proximity" as BANK <<db>>
  component "kingThreatened" as HOT <<app>>
  component "turn · income tiers → horizon 5\nprojectedBank(bank, turn, 5)" as HORIZON <<app>>
}

package "Strategic economy" {
  component "strategies/economy.ts\ndeploys()" as ECO <<app>>
  component "deployLookahead.ts\nbestDeploySequence(horizon:5)\np+p+q vs n+b+r on budget 11" as LOOK <<app>>
  package "Dials" {
    component "QUEEN_FINISH 3200\nwinning ∧ gap = 0 ∧ bank ≥ 9" as SHIP <<app>>
    component "HIDDEN_GUARD 1450\ngap > 0 (cheese window)" as GUARD <<app>>
    component "skip p/n\nwinning ∧ gap = 0 ∧ bank < 9 ∧ horizonBank ≥ 9" as SAVE <<app>>
    component "SHIP_WARP_READY 800\n(+ SHIP_HORIZON_BONUS 600)\nCC guess within warp reach" as WARP <<app>>
    component "direct spawn crush\ntrade × (1 + UNIT_COST[victim])\n**not** deploy-reach" as CRUSH <<app>>
  }
}

package "Deploy choice" {
  database "Command Center\nB: spawn unit" as DROP <<db>>
}

KVS ARROW_MAIN ECO : gap = known − (scouted − captured)
BANK ARROW_OPTIONAL ECO : deployPolicy (naive)
HORIZON ARROW_MAIN ECO : budget over 5 turns
HOT ARROW_OPTIONAL ECO : survival outranks saving
ECO ARROW_MAIN LOOK : score sequences on projected budget
ECO ARROW_OPTIONAL SHIP : close the game
ECO ARROW_OPTIONAL GUARD : rook guard vs unseen
ECO ARROW_OPTIONAL SAVE : bank toward a ship within horizon
LOOK ARROW_MAIN DROP : first unit of best sequence
SHIP ARROW_MAIN DROP : drop ""q"" at King perimeter
GUARD ARROW_MAIN DROP : rook / shore pawns
SAVE ARROW_MAIN DROP : wait (no light drops)
ECO ARROW_OPTIONAL WARP : ccIntel.focus one away\nor on a clear line
ECO ARROW_OPTIONAL CRUSH : ring square holds an enemy unit
WARP ARROW_MAIN DROP : drop ""q"" ready to jump
CRUSH ARROW_MAIN DROP : land on the victim

note bottom
  **Rules, in priority order:**
  * ""kingThreatened"" — survival dials dominate (unchanged from naive).
  * ""gap > 0"" — hidden enemy material (promotion runner / cheese):
    defense outranks saving; rook guard ""HIDDEN_GUARD""; ship rush cancelled.
  * ""winning ∧ gap = 0"" — our board + captures exceed what the enemy
    knows: rush the BattleShip once the bank pays for a queen
    (""QUEEN_FINISH"") and skip pawn / hoverbike drops that delay it —
    saving only when the ship is reachable within 5 turns
    (""horizonBank ≥ 9"").
  * **Deploy budget over 5:** projects stored minerals after 5 turns of
    income (capped 12) and scores sequences e.g. ""p+p+q"" (1+1+9=11) vs
    ""n+b+r"" (3+3+5=11) when projected budget is 11 in 3 turns; the
    immediate deploy is the first unit of the best horizon sequence
    (discounted, horizon-aligned bonus).
  * otherwise — naive deploy mix, unchanged.
end note

note as N_WARP
  **The warp-ready bonus, and whose guess it trusts.** A Battleship drop is
  worth ""SHIP_HORIZON_BONUS + SHIP_WARP_READY"" (600 + 800) when the CC guess
  is one square from a lit tile, or on a clear line from one — because the ship
  can then Tactical Jump straight into check next turn. The distance test is
  ""chebyshev"", shared from ""ai/context/geometry.ts""; it replaced an inline
  ""charCodeAt"" pair that computed the same thing a third way.

  This is the **only** consumer of the cross-ply CC posterior
  (""ctx.ccIntel?.focus""). Every other CC-aimed weight reads the one-turn
  centroid instead, and in arena runs the posterior is discarded each ply — so
  today this bonus effectively fires off the home prior. See ""../cc-focus.puml"".
end note

note as N_CRUSH
  **Deploying to crush is a *score*, not a proof.** A ring square holding an
  enemy unit earns ""trade × (1 + UNIT_COST[victim])"" and then competes with
  every other deploy that turn, which is the right shape for a preference the
  tuning is meant to move.

  The mirror-image question — can the **opponent** deploy onto a square and
  recapture there — is a deterministic boolean and lives in
  ""board/deploy-reach.ts"" instead. Conflating the two would turn one of them
  into the wrong kind of answer, so the split is deliberate and load-bearing;
  ""_spec/packages/starchess-core/deploy-reach.puml"" states the non-goal from
  the other side.
end note

note as N_LANDINGS
  <color:#CB2000>**OPEN — four derivations of one rule.**</color>
  "Which ring squares may a deploy land on" is answered in four places, and
  only the first matches the validator (""rules/specials/adjacent.ts"" +
  ""rules/validation.ts"": own colour blocked, **any** King blocked, an enemy
  non-King crushed):

  | site | filter | own colour | enemy non-King | enemy CC | verdict |
  | ""board/deploy-reach.ts"" ""deployTargets"" | colour + King test | blocked | **kept** | blocked | correct |
  | ""ai/strategies/economy.ts"" ""deploys"" (naive) | ""!map.has(at)"" | blocked | **blocked** | blocked | too strict |
  | ""ai/strategic/strategies/economy.ts"" ""deploys"" | mine only | **kept** | kept | **kept** | too loose |
  | ""ai/strategic/deployLookahead.ts"" ""bestScoreForUnit"" | ""!map.has(at)"" | blocked | **blocked** | blocked | too strict |

  **Consequences, in order of cost.** The strategic generator being too loose
  costs only wasted candidates (see the note beside it). The two strict sites
  cost real play: requiring an empty tile means neither the naive economy nor
  the horizon lookahead ever proposes a crush deploy, so a legal and often
  strong move is simply never played. Worst of the four, the strategic
  generator and its own lookahead disagree, so a horizon sequence can be scored
  on tiles the generator would not have offered.

  The strategic generator's ring filter tests hostile mines and nothing else,
  so it is the "too loose" row above by omission rather than by intent. The
  binding statement of the rule is the validator; the executable one is
  ""src/__tests__/deploy-reach.test.ts"", at the cases "keeps an enemy occupant
  (the deploy crushes it) but drops our own" and "drops every King square — an
  enemy Command Center cannot be crushed". **Not fixed on this branch.**
end note

note as N_DEAD
  **What the cleanup removed.** A dead ""_isOpenFile"" helper and the comment
  that described the open-file gate it never actually implemented are gone, so
  the file no longer documents a rule the code does not have. A tank deploy is
  therefore preferred by ""ROOK_AFTER_KNIGHTS"" and ""HIDDEN_GUARD"" alone, with
  no file-openness term anywhere in the pure core.

  A separate closed-file cap does still exist, but it is an **arena** concern
  in ""players/strategic.ts"" — it caps how far Stockfish may boost a tank drop,
  and it never changes the deterministic score.
end note

ECO .. N_WARP
ECO .. N_CRUSH
ECO .. N_LANDINGS
ECO .. N_DEAD
@enduml